Licensed under the MIT License.
https://github.com/lerd-env/lerd
https://lerd.sh

VALET preserves the engine's binary name, API paths, configuration files,
containers, volumes, images, certificates, project markers and persisted data.
The engine is installed and licensed separately.

Themes
------

Min Dark and Min Light theme JSON are based on Min Theme.
Copyright (c) 2018-2021 Miguel Solorio
Licensed under the MIT License.
https://github.com/miguelsolorio/min-theme

The theme JSON files are used as the visual source of truth. VALET's adapter
derives semantic CSS variables and an xterm palette without creating a new
brand palette.

Desktop dependencies
--------------------

Electron, React, React DOM, Vite, xterm.js, the xterm fit addon, lucide-react,
TypeScript, Vitest and electron-builder are distributed under their respective
licenses. Their license texts are available in `node_modules/<package>` and in
the packaged application's dependency notices.

Not included
------------

- The Lerd engine binary.
- PHP, Podman, Nginx, MySQL, PostgreSQL, Redis or other runtime services.
- phpMyAdmin. VALET retires it from active features; a pre-existing container
  can be removed explicitly but its data is not deleted by VALET.
- Any user project, database dump, certificate private key or credential.

Name note
---------

Laravel Valet also uses the command name `valet`. VALET's installer deliberately
refuses to overwrite an existing unrelated `valet` executable. This project is
not affiliated with Laravel, Lerd or the Min Theme author beyond the license and
compatibility notices above.

